From 7da2330350964c6f605bd105b03d72c0c5d08789 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 00:23:41 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 192/192] pmdomain: mediatek: verify OVL physical off before
 retiring boot votes

Use an optional always-on MT6897 SPM syscon to observe OVL PWR_CON after
successful HWV-off, before releasing the complete ordinary root enable
references. Require both ACKs, RST_B and both PWR_ON bits clear, with ISO
and CLK_DIS set. Invalid, mixed or failed reads preserve boot ownership
without quarantining an otherwise healthy domain. Log bounded initial
failures and eventual successful observations.

Resolve the static top boot-owner handle after all root preparation and
before any domain initialization or hardware request. Pure preflight
unwind releases enrollment before parent readiness; successful and
quarantined controllers retain it. Keep the physical offsets and bank
identity explicit and independent of clock-reference counts. Point T880's
optional phandle to the SPM syscon, avoiding its dependent child domain.

Reject clocks, resets, hardware locks and domain dependencies before
creating the status-only map. In particular syscon map creation could
otherwise deassert a reset. Existing HWV map reset handling is unchanged.

Link: https://github.com/MiCode/MTK_kernel_device_modules/blob/3c4ccd07d5624879555ec710c11bb8818e5cb5c6/drivers/clk/mediatek/clkchk-mt6897.c
